# Actual local drift handling
The actual local desired/live files are configuration artifacts, not a GCP service or Argo controller. Plan is read-only. Every difference needs a retain/revert decision. Apply exits 2 before writing if decisions are missing, desired changed, or live bytes no longer match the approved observation or deterministic approved result. Preserve observed live object, exact before hash and desired hash; changed live data after review requires another review.
Retain keeps approved emergency values; revert permits convergence only for that field. Never rewrite desired to silently legalize unknown changes. Retained values still require reviewed source updates with incident evidence, owner and expiry; no Git commits occur here. The editable approval JSON is exercise input, not authentication or access control; real platforms must use their existing trusted process.
An alternative is supported temporary pause of only affected reconciliation with a bounded review window. Blanket overwrites, unlimited pauses and unreviewed source edits are wrong. Second apply is byte-stable. Preserve before-state for rollback and delete only private artifacts.


